    "chunk_size_bytes": 1408,
    "chunk_text": "The certificate was officially handed over by the Deputy Minister of Environment to AFL\u2019s Director and Chief Executive Officer, Ashan Nissanka, in the presence of senior government officials and other stakeholders. This achievement marks a significant milestone in AFL\u2019s sustainability journey and demonstrates strong alignment with the Central Bank of Sri Lanka\u2019s (CBSL) Roadmap for Sustainable Finance.\n\nAchieving certification across all three emission scopes reflects AFL\u2019s robust governance framework and its integrated approach to sustainability, risk management, and operational oversight. This initiative supports CBSL\u2019s guidance for financial institutions to identify, measure, monitor, and manage climate-related and environmental risks within business models.\n\nObtaining ISO 14064-1:2018 verification will be a strategic enabler that strengthens transparency, data integrity, and climate resilience. It also reinforces AFL\u2019s commitment towards consistent environmental stewardship, and long-term value creation with sustainability as a core factor, adds Mr Nissanka in conclusion.\n\nCharles Sturt University \u2013 Colombo advances Sri Lanka\u2019s higher education agenda with high-level roundtable\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
